{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1727","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1727","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1727\",\"parent_revision\":\"d222e37d11cab39ee1cc1b1964ff4c21a0c39963699945f81f60cf268ef13915\",\"root_revision\":\"d222e37d11cab39ee1cc1b1964ff4c21a0c39963699945f81f60cf268ef13915\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `artifact_provider.py` readable | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` |\\n| 2 | Factory/registry lines 836, 889, 1091, 1138 contain the selector | AVAILABLE | Item description |\\n| 3 | `GithubArtifactProvider` abstract Protocol at lines 310-345 | AVAILABLE | Item description (round 2 findings) |\\n| 4 | Concrete gist implementation at lines 531-575 named `GitLabArtifactProvider` | AVAILABLE | Item description |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 investigation task with all source locations specified.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Chore. Investigation only. No code changes. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- The factory or registry that selects the concrete ArtifactProvider at runtime is identified by reading `artifact_provider.py` lines 836, 889, 1091, and 1138\\n- The concrete class that handles GitHub-backed artifact operations is named with certainty\\n- If `GitLabArtifactProvider` (lines 531-575) actually handles GitHub gist operations, that naming inconsistency is documented as a follow-up item\\n- Findings written to `.tmp/scratch/reports/artifact-provider-audit.md` with exact line citations\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 lines 310-345, 531-575, 836, 889, 1091, 1138 (read-only investigation)\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/artifact-provider-audit.md` \u2014 findings document\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a backlog_core developer, I need to know which `ArtifactProvider` class actually executes in production when the DH state points at a GitHub repo so I can trust artifact read/write operations and fix any misattributions in verification documents.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **unknown: which artifactprovider class runs in production against github?** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u5\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification-round2.md` \u00a7Q2\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Matters\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe chunked-append work depends on knowing which provider to modify. Modifying the wrong class ships a no-op. The naming confusion also suggests the class hierarchy is itself a source of maintenance risk.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nTwo rounds of verification against `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` produced mismatched attributions:\\n\\n- Round 1 (`backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u5) attributed lines 503-537 (containing `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})`) to the \\\"GitHub backend\\\".\\n- Round 2 (`backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification-round2.md` \u00a7Q2) found that `GithubArtifactProvider` at lines 310-345 is an abstract Protocol with `...` bodies, and the concrete gist-based implementation at lines 531-575 is actually `GitLabArtifactProvider`.\\n\\nThe factory or registry that selects the concrete provider at runtime has not been read. Until that is confirmed, it is unclear which class actually executes when the DH state points at a GitHub repo \u2014 a GitLab-named class that happens to use PyGithub, a second concrete GitHub class not yet examined (lines 836, 889, 1091, 1138 are flagged in round 2 as unread), or a dispatcher that picks per-remote.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Verified code audit 2026-04-12 \u2014 chunked-io-verification-round2.md (c15)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3bcfa02a03d79e2409d7610d0c817a314f9409b28396572551f3704449d7be90\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS-SOg\"}"}